# Drilling onward from a pin, instead of leaving it.
#
# Entering a pin is the one jump in this app, so it records the screen it left
# and `back` honours that first. Every other move clears the record, because
# every other move is one step and its parent is where it came from.
#
# `drilldown` enters a pin and escs straight back out, which uses the record and
# empties it. Nothing walked the other path: enter a pin, go somewhere else, and
# then press esc. If a move forgot to clear the record, that esc jumps to the
# first screen from four levels down instead of going up one.
#
# The last frame must be the directions, not the first screen.
cache ../cache.db
date 2026-09-11
time 08:00
offset -04:00
size 100 14

# Into the pin's board. This is the jump that sets the record.
enter

# Away from it, without using the record. `/` is a move like any other.
key /

# Down past the pin to Bus, then all the way to a stop list.
down
enter
type 44
enter

# The direction is named. A bare enter takes whatever the slice sorts first.
type hurdman
enter

# One level up. The stop list belongs to a direction, so this is the directions.
esc
